00:03:27.789 --> 00:03:30.917
But Stephen first off I'm curious,

00:03:30.917 --> 00:03:33.594
why do you think people have a hard time

00:03:33.594 --> 00:03:36.067
being their true self and
having that confidence

00:03:36.067 --> 00:03:38.383
to project that and use
that and tell their story,

00:03:38.383 --> 00:03:40.784
what do you think is
the reason that people

00:03:40.784 --> 00:03:43.223
have a hard time with it so much?

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:46.728
- I think part of it is a fear of failure,

00:03:46.728 --> 00:03:48.093
and when I look at start-ups,

00:03:48.093 --> 00:03:50.559
what 90% of them actually sadly fail,

00:03:50.559 --> 00:03:52.392
only 10% succeed,

00:03:54.526 --> 00:03:56.499
also if I look at the optimism,

00:03:56.499 --> 00:04:00.389
particularly in the 18
through 30 year olds

00:04:00.389 --> 00:04:01.772
in terms of entrepreneurs,

00:04:01.772 --> 00:04:05.939
95% of 'em have a real
belief in their own success

00:04:07.017 --> 00:04:09.162
but I just look at my own kind of career

00:04:09.162 --> 00:04:10.360
as an entrepreneur Evan

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:13.104
and I think there is some
periods in your life,

00:04:13.104 --> 00:04:14.993
where there are seeds of doubt

00:04:14.993 --> 00:04:18.680
and it's at those times
where you really need

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:21.059
to galvanize your
confidence to be successful.

00:04:21.059 --> 00:04:23.099
It's just human nature,

00:04:23.099 --> 00:04:25.928
all of us have got that vulnerability

00:04:25.928 --> 00:04:28.050
but I think you really need to dig into

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.883
your own authenticity.

00:04:30.783 --> 00:04:32.972
Dig also into your core values.

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:36.318
What is your dream, how are
you going to change the world?

00:04:36.318 --> 00:04:38.655
What are you going to
do for your audience?

00:04:38.655 --> 00:04:41.856
If you stick to that then
the dark days come along

00:04:41.856 --> 00:04:45.032
and you hit some bumps in the road.

00:04:45.032 --> 00:04:47.723
Then you can really kind of double down

00:04:47.723 --> 00:04:50.634
and it builds your self confidence

00:04:50.634 --> 00:04:53.963
and we can talk also
about during the broadcast

00:04:53.963 --> 00:04:55.801
how we kind of connect
with other people to.

00:04:55.801 --> 00:04:58.120
To galvanize our
confidence and build it up.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:01.207
Just an example from my career,

00:05:01.207 --> 00:05:05.601
about 20 years ago when
I was early stage CEO,

00:05:05.601 --> 00:05:09.585
we were doin' a big pilot for a company.

00:05:09.585 --> 00:05:11.058
We kind of bet the ranch.

00:05:11.058 --> 00:05:12.640
We bet the company on this

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:15.879
and it was the light Fortune 500 company.

00:05:15.879 --> 00:05:18.127
We put all our best people on this pilot

00:05:18.127 --> 00:05:20.831
and we actually turned
down other business,

00:05:20.831 --> 00:05:25.215
and the sad thing is
the guy who was the VP

00:05:25.215 --> 00:05:27.552
leading that project got moved,

00:05:27.552 --> 00:05:30.528
left the company and we lost our sponsor

00:05:30.528 --> 00:05:32.816
and the pilot got killed.

00:05:32.816 --> 00:05:34.613
We were doing really well

00:05:34.613 --> 00:05:36.955
and it was so demotivating for the team

00:05:36.955 --> 00:05:40.011
'cause they worked crazy 80 hours a week,

00:05:40.011 --> 00:05:41.948
they'd gone the extra mile,

00:05:41.948 --> 00:05:44.504
it was a real story of human sacrifice

00:05:44.504 --> 00:05:46.483
and blood sweat and tears.

00:05:46.483 --> 00:05:48.771
When I look back what did it do?

00:05:48.771 --> 00:05:52.354
It actually, we had
some hard conversation,

00:05:54.098 --> 00:05:56.348
we were runnin' out of cash

00:05:57.306 --> 00:05:59.609
and we did things like cut our own wages,

00:05:59.609 --> 00:06:03.299
we sacrificed salaries,
practically worked for nothing

00:06:03.299 --> 00:06:04.849
and what it meant was,

00:06:04.849 --> 00:06:07.500
when we tasted success for the first time,

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.144
boy did it taste sweet

00:06:09.144 --> 00:06:10.449
but it took us honestly,

00:06:10.449 --> 00:06:12.504
when we looked at the
business plan we put together,

00:06:12.504 --> 00:06:15.205
it probably took us about 12 months longer

00:06:15.205 --> 00:06:18.705
because we hit a wall, lost that customer,

00:06:19.834 --> 00:06:22.571
we'd sacrificed the
opportunity cost of not working

00:06:22.571 --> 00:06:24.359
while the business was immense

00:06:24.359 --> 00:06:26.403
and it meant we really had to double down,

00:06:26.403 --> 00:06:30.434
now why did we have the
confidence to do that?

00:06:30.434 --> 00:06:33.596
One is we really believed in this case

00:06:33.596 --> 00:06:35.522
it was a product we were selling,

00:06:35.522 --> 00:06:37.198
we really believed it solved

00:06:37.198 --> 00:06:39.535
a massive need for our customers.

00:06:39.535 --> 00:06:43.381
Two is we really knew that particularly,

00:06:43.381 --> 00:06:44.398
actually through the pilot,

00:06:44.398 --> 00:06:48.626
when we saw the cost it
took out of this business

00:06:48.626 --> 00:06:52.618
in the Fortune 500 and how they
could be way more efficient.

00:06:52.618 --> 00:06:55.835
That it had a compelling benefit.

00:06:55.835 --> 00:06:58.797
Thirdly, when we looked around the room

00:06:58.797 --> 00:07:02.464
on a pretty dark day
when we lost the pilot,

00:07:03.836 --> 00:07:05.657
we just looked at each other and said,

00:07:05.657 --> 00:07:07.806
actually do we believe in each other?

00:07:07.806 --> 00:07:11.055
Have we got a great idea,
are we going to double down,

00:07:11.055 --> 00:07:13.477
maybe draw no salaries at all

00:07:13.477 --> 00:07:15.436
and go the long haul.

00:07:15.436 --> 00:07:19.197
We said yeah we would and in
reality it took us longer.

00:07:19.197 --> 00:07:21.409
Now why I'm tellin' you
that is I think you have

00:07:21.409 --> 00:07:24.314
to look at your inner
self you really do need

00:07:24.314 --> 00:07:26.858
to challenge yourselves as entrepreneurs

00:07:26.858 --> 00:07:30.261
within your audience and you
got to believe in your idea,

00:07:30.261 --> 00:07:32.412
you got to believe it
will make a difference,

00:07:32.412 --> 00:07:34.447
and you've got to stay true to yourself

00:07:34.447 --> 00:07:36.787
and absolutely have that confidence

00:07:36.787 --> 00:07:39.694
to be authentic and honest,

00:07:39.694 --> 00:07:42.176
to go the long haul on it,

00:07:42.176 --> 00:07:44.135
if you got the belief and you got a dream

00:07:44.135 --> 00:07:47.062
and you know it can change the world.

00:07:47.062 --> 00:07:49.118
That's where you get your confidence from

00:07:49.118 --> 00:07:51.278
and reality of all of us honestly,

00:07:51.278 --> 00:07:52.598
were the aspirations and dreams

00:07:52.598 --> 00:07:54.574
when we put business plans together,

00:07:54.574 --> 00:07:57.712
sometimes it just takes longer
sometimes it takes longer

00:07:57.712 --> 00:08:01.441
and the small entrepreneurs out there,

00:08:01.441 --> 00:08:03.142
the entrepreneurs who double down

00:08:03.142 --> 00:08:07.671
or actually change the
idea to pick a new idea

00:08:07.671 --> 00:08:08.814
to win the next time.

00:08:08.814 --> 00:08:11.418
'Cause then you put your lesson to work

00:08:11.418 --> 00:08:13.941
and you create the next business.

00:08:13.941 --> 00:08:16.322
- I love it you're already
gaining tons of love

00:08:16.322 --> 00:08:18.493
in the chat for the
opening statement there,

