around the challenges women face

00:53:03.359 --> 00:53:07.196
in terms of establishing
an entrepreneurs career

00:53:07.196 --> 00:53:11.342
and some of the sub conscious
barriers that are out there,

00:53:11.342 --> 00:53:15.509
it's a book called What
Works, we'll send it to you,

00:53:17.459 --> 00:53:19.611
so we'll put it out on social media

00:53:19.611 --> 00:53:20.776
but I think it's a really cool book.

00:53:20.776 --> 00:53:22.193
Why do I like it?

00:53:23.206 --> 00:53:26.462
I like it 'cause it challenges
so many assumptions,

00:53:26.462 --> 00:53:28.545
now it's a bit different,

00:53:29.666 --> 00:53:31.280
it's not related, well it
is related to entrepreneurs,

00:53:31.280 --> 00:53:33.323
it's related to life, it's a life book

00:53:33.323 --> 00:53:34.256
so I think it's pretty cool.

00:53:34.256 --> 00:53:35.518
There's loads of books you know

00:53:35.518 --> 00:53:38.471
you can do From Good to Great,

00:53:38.471 --> 00:53:41.478
Branson's books are fantastic.

00:53:41.478 --> 00:53:44.516
What you tend to find with
these business books honestly,

00:53:44.516 --> 00:53:47.808
is you can read 'em but
there's normally two or three

00:53:47.808 --> 00:53:51.891
great ideas that you know
make huge common sense,

00:53:53.771 --> 00:53:54.787
it's about trusting your instincts

00:53:54.787 --> 00:53:57.268
and when you pick out these
nuggets in these books,

00:53:57.268 --> 00:53:59.022
and obviously you can apply them

00:53:59.022 --> 00:54:02.605
they're injections that
give you new energy

00:54:04.010 --> 00:54:05.643
and probably greater confidence

00:54:05.643 --> 00:54:08.648
and really encourage you
to support your conviction

00:54:08.648 --> 00:54:11.442
but I think the thing that
you should be thinkin' of

00:54:11.442 --> 00:54:13.577
is what's your book?

00:54:13.577 --> 00:54:16.736
What's your book of your great idea

00:54:16.736 --> 00:54:18.992
and how you brought that to market

00:54:18.992 --> 00:54:21.331
and actually when you start your companies

00:54:21.331 --> 00:54:22.955
and when you grow your companies,

00:54:22.955 --> 00:54:25.406
it is worth thinking about
the chapters of the book

00:54:25.406 --> 00:54:27.185
that you're going to write one day

00:54:27.185 --> 00:54:30.178
about how you built a product,

00:54:30.178 --> 00:54:34.006
changed the world, stuck to your big dream

00:54:34.006 --> 00:54:37.089
and was always very true to yourself,

00:54:37.953 --> 00:54:39.801
how you hire great people around you,

00:54:39.801 --> 00:54:40.908
all these sort of things,

00:54:40.908 --> 00:54:43.553
'cause when you do this it builds culture

00:54:43.553 --> 00:54:46.227
and in your companies it's
great to have that culture

00:54:46.227 --> 00:54:49.135
and that's the reason why
people want to work for you,

00:54:49.135 --> 00:54:50.635
and be around you.

00:54:52.009 --> 00:54:54.897
Read lots of books, get lots of ideas,

00:54:54.897 --> 00:54:58.721
if there's amazing mentors
out there, learn from them

00:54:58.721 --> 00:55:01.972
but think about writing your own book

00:55:01.972 --> 00:55:04.431
and make it different,
make it challenging,

00:55:04.431 --> 00:55:09.147
make it the essence of your
big idea but also who you are.

00:55:09.147 --> 00:55:10.846
- I like it, I like it.

00:55:10.846 --> 00:55:13.011
Stephen when are you
comin' out with your book,

00:55:13.011 --> 00:55:14.708
I want the Stephen Kelly book,

00:55:14.708 --> 00:55:17.174
